On Dec 6, 9:56 am, Kent Paul Dolan <xanth...@well.com> wrote:
> Could I have Engraved Elbereth while engulphed, to
> get double use out of the wand charge, as opposed to
> just zapping the worm from its guts for the
> guaranteed hit?

Unfortunately, you can't engrave while engulfed by a monster. If
engulfed by a non-corporeal creature (i.e. vortices), you get:

"You can't reach the floor."

Corporeal monsters like purple worms or lurkers give the much more
amusing:

"What would you write? 'Jonah was here'?"

Which reminds me, there are some funny messages related to being
engulfed. Try searching, looking/feeling for items, or trying to pick
up an item while engulfed.

In this case, your wand(s) were probably the best and only options.
I'm not sure if the wand of fire would have done much for you, if it's
any consolation. Wizmode testing implies that it tends to take around
4 zaps of a wand of fire to kill a purple worm. It's not likely that
you would have survived that long with 36 HP.

A better option, if you hand one, would be a wand of opening or a wand
of digging. Either would have forced the purple worm to immediately
release you. You could then possibly engrave the E word or run away.
Or, if it was a wand of digging, you could dig straight down and
escape through the floor. Neither is a sure thing, though. Unless you
have sufficient speed, the purple worm might just release and re-
engulf you before you have a chance to act.

